.de QU.ie t ``\\$1''\\$2.el "\\$1"\\$2...TH NOBS 6 "10 March 1988" "" "Local UNIX Programmer's Manual".SH NAMEnobs \- cribbage game.SH SYNOPSIS.B nobs[.B \-v].SH DESCRIPTIONWith no arguments,.I cribbageplays screen-oriented games of cribbage with you.You select cards by typing a letter from.QU ato.QU f .The program keeps score.Game is 121 points..PPIf you specify.BR \-v ,.I cribbageprints the version number and exits..SH WARNINGThis program has been around a long time, having started out in FORTRAN on a CDC 6400.It is a dangerous opponent..SH AUTHORG. L. Sicherman  (ihnp4\^!\^odyssey\^!\^gls)